timestamp=2026-10-29T11:12:54.981Z level=INFO run=f162cdeb message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat > result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/payloads/redirect-uri.txt <<'EOF'\n# Payload (URL-encoded redirectURI value)\n/%09/evil.com/\n# decoded form inside redirectURI query parameter:\n/\\t/evil.com/\n\n# Full proof URL (already-authenticated victim):\nhttps://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fevil.com%2F\n\n# Full proof URL (victim logs in):\nhttps://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fexample.com%2F\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-10-29T11:12:54.981Z level=INFO run=f162cdeb message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat > result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/evidence/observation.md <<'EOF'\n# Evidence — Open redirect via auth `redirectURI`\n\nAll times UTC, 2026-10-29. Test account B (`testt456`, account 3001021825).\n\n## A. Already-authenticated victim (one click, no login prompt)\n\n1. Browser page 2 was logged in as account B and sat on\n   `https://console.byteplus.com/home`.\n2. Navigated to:\n   `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fevil.com%2F`\n3. After ~4s the top-level document was:\n   `{\"url\":\"https://evil.com/\",\"title\":\"Evil.Com - We get it...Daily.\"}`\n\nNo credentials were re-entered. The login page auto-redirected the\nauthenticated session to the attacker-controlled external origin.\n\n## B. Victim logs in (login flow)\n\n1. Fresh isolated browser context opened:\n   `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fexample.com%2F`\n2. Logged in with disposable test account B\n   (`testt456` / `Acd3423@#345`).\n3. One second after submit the top-level document was:\n   `{\"t\":1,\"url\":\"https://example.com/\"}`\n4. Preserved network log on that page:\n   - `POST https://console.byteplus.com/api/passport/login/mixtureLogin?...` [200]\n   - request `referer` header:\n     `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fexample.com%2F`\n   - request body: `{\"Identity\":\"testt456\",\"Password\":\"...\",\"EventName\":\"AuthAccountWithPassword\"}`\n   - followed by `GET https://example.com/` [200]\n5. Login API response body (including `Result.RedirectPath`) was no longer\n   buffered by CDP, but the runtime navigation and the preserved\n   `GET https://example.com/` document request prove the redirect target.\n\n## C. Why the payload bypasses the whitelist\n\n`redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fexample.com%2F` decodes to `/\\t/example.com/`.\n- Literal absolute URLs (`https://example.com/`) and `//example.com/` and\n  `/\\example.com/` were rejected (landed on `/home`).\n- The tab character survives server-side validation because the value still\n  starts with a single `/`.\n- The browser strips the raw tab when resolving the URL:\n  `new URL('/\\t/example.com/', 'https://console.byteplus.com').href`\n  == `https://example.com/` (verified in-page, char codes 47,9,47,...).\n- Therefore `location.assign()`/navigation resolves the \"relative\" path to an\n  external origin.\n\n## Negative escalation check\n\n`redirectURI=javascript%3Awindow.__redirjs%3D1` did **not** execute\nJavaScript; the browser landed on a `chrome-error://chromewebdata/`\n403 page. `javascript:` execution is not confirmed.\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
timestamp=2026-10-29T11:12:54.981Z level=INFO run=f162cdeb message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="cat > result/findings/VULN-20261029-001/report.md <<'EOF'\n# VULN-20261029-001 — Open redirect via auth `redirectURI` (tab-character bypass)\n\n- Status: **Confirmed** (open redirect)\n- Type: Open Redirect (client-side / auth flow)\n- Asset: `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/`\n- Severity: Medium\n- Authentication: unauthenticated (pre-login link); automatic for an\n  already-authenticated victim\n- Tested at: 2026-10-29T11:11:00Z\n\n## Summary\n\nThe login page accepts a `redirectURI` query parameter and, after a successful\nlogin (or immediately when the visitor already has a session), navigates the\ntop-level document to that value. Absolute URLs, protocol-relative URLs\n(`//host`) and `/\\host` are rejected, but a tab character inserted after the\nleading slash (`/%09/evil.com/`) bypasses the same-origin validation. Browsers\nstrip the tab while parsing the URL, so `/\\t/evil.com/` resolves to\n`https://evil.com/`.\n\nImpact: an attacker can send a link that, once the victim is logged in (or\nright after they log in), silently takes them from the trusted\n`console.byteplus.com` origin to an attacker-controlled site. This enables\ncredible phishing, OAuth/token-harvesting pages reached from a trusted link,\nand generic open-redirect abuse. No JavaScript executes on the target origin,\nso this is not reported as XSS.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. While logged in to `console.byteplus.com` (test account B), open\n   `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fevil.com%2F`.\n2. Observe the top-level document become `https://evil.com/` with no prompt.\n3. Alternatively, in a clean browser open\n   `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/?redirectURI=%2F%09%2Fexample.com%2F`,\n   log in, and observe navigation to `https://example.com/`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `evidence/observation.md` — exact URLs, observed final URLs, network\n  requests, and char-code verification.\n- `payloads/redirect-uri.txt` — payloads.\n\n## Affected code\n\n`https://res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/vconsole-auth/byteplus/static/js/1.0.0.2811/main.adbc4e5a.js`\n- login component reads `redirectURI` (`t.get(\"redirectURI\")`) and the app\n  performs `location.assign(...)` with the resulting destination.\n\n## Remediation\n\n- Resolve the `redirectURI` server-side with a strict URL parser and require\n  the normalized origin to equal `https://console.byteplus.com`; reject any\n  value containing C0 controls, backslashes, or leading `//`.\n- Prefer an allowlist of relative paths and re-serialize the path instead of\n  echoing the raw input.\n- Do not auto-redirect already-authenticated users from the login page based on\n  an unvalidated query parameter.\n\n## Notification decision\n\n`Confirmed-vuln.txt: excluded — Rule 9 excludes plain open redirects; a\ndangerous javascript: URL was not achievable (verified, see evidence).`\nEOF" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
